From caccf555ed266564726efaf272f9554f49913a98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasiliy Stelmachenok <ventureo@cachyos.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:40:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] Revert "PCI: Skip Target Speed quirk on clamped ports
 with no link"

For some reason it causes hang at boot on some hardware:

https://paste.cachyos.org/p/49a2487.log

This reverts commit e50dc23c030f7051a88ca1362cc3c970ecb57c15.
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index 9e407c449..b09f27f78 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -108,11 +108,7 @@ int pcie_failed_link_retrain(struct pci_dev *dev)
 
 	pcie_capability_read_word(dev, PCI_EXP_LNKSTA, &lnksta);
 	pcie_capability_read_word(dev, PCI_EXP_LNKCTL2, &oldlnkctl2);
-	if (lnksta & PCI_EXP_LNKSTA_DLLLA) {
-		;
-	} else if (PCIE_LNKCTL2_TLS2SPEED(oldlnkctl2) == PCIE_SPEED_2_5GT) {
-		return ret;
-	} else if (pcie_lbms_seen(dev, lnksta)) {
+	if (!(lnksta & PCI_EXP_LNKSTA_DLLLA) && pcie_lbms_seen(dev, lnksta)) {
 		pci_info(dev, "broken device, retraining non-functional downstream link at 2.5GT/s\n");
 		ret = pcie_set_target_speed(dev, PCIE_SPEED_2_5GT, false);
 		if (ret)
